WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.400
Data rarely follows a single path from one place to another.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.200
Instead it is split into packets, and each packet finds its own way.

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:12.200
Routers choose the next hop as the traffic arrives.

4
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:16.000
When one route becomes crowded, another route can take its place.

5
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.400
That is why the network keeps working as it grows.